# Production build-time configuration for the Clavis frontend.
#
# Vite bakes VITE_API_URL into the static bundle at COMPILE TIME (not a runtime
# setting). The app is single-origin: the browser reaches the API at the SAME
# host, path-routed under /api by the reverse proxy.
#
# Therefore VITE_API_URL is intentionally EMPTY -> the SPA uses relative,
# same-origin requests (`/api/...`). This is host-agnostic (works on the prod
# domain, staging, or a private network name) and satisfies the `connect-src 'self'`
# CSP. Set a value here ONLY if the API ever moves to a different origin.
#
# NOTE: the Docker build also defaults VITE_API_URL to empty (see Dockerfile).
# A non-empty value in either place must be a full different-origin URL, never
# `http://localhost` — that ships a bundle whose every API call fails in prod.
VITE_API_URL=
